data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work without requiring `unsafe` context:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint`/`nuint` are 8 bytes each. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context (since the size isn't fixed at compile time) — use `nint.Size` instead in safe code.
